									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 950.0, 29.0, 396.0, 194.0 ],
									"text" : "There are three parts to this gen~ file: a part that makes beep sounds, a part that makes hi-hat hits, and a part that makes a \"charging up\" sort of sound.\n\nThe charging sound is the first sound I added to my gen. I accidentaly created the \"charging up\" sound while editing one of the sample patches when I encorporated in the second, but added a modulo 10, which made the cycle progressivly get faster over the course of 10 seconds, and then reset. I liked this part, and decided to make it the focus of my project, and added the other sounds as the background. \n\nAlso during the time I spent making this project, I noticed that I had a lot more issues than normal, most likely due to increased gen~ size making it more complex. Something to keep in mind for the future. "
								}

